      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm so confused as to why downgrading is seen as a good idea. Imposters are vastly inferior to fallbacks in every way. Period. All the work I put into my fallbacks going to waste is incredibly frustrating for me.\n\nImposter generation is a total mess at this point. They are exceedingly ugly, too. Like a bowl of mashed potatoes. In a game that, for many, can revolve around aesthetics, this is a massive step back. I find myself shutting off imposters because the gray robot is more appealing to me. They lack visemes, gestures, are ugly, and often naked or have clothing issues.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
